\partial_t u − kappa \Delta u + u^3 =0, in \Omega,
u=0 on \partial \Omega,

Implicit Euler at step 
R(u^{n+1}) = (M + \Delta t \kappa K) u^{n+1} + \Delta t \, M (u^{n+1})^3 - M u^n = 0

Newton requires Jacobian:
J = (M + \Delta t \kappa K) + \Delta t M (3 (u^{n+1})^2)

(where the nonlinear part is assembled element-wise)
